### ==============================================================================
### Payload CMS - RBAC REST Client Suite (Skeleton Template)
### OWASP Top 10 Compliant: Zero Hardcoded Credentials (CWE-798 / CWE-359)
### ==============================================================================
### USAGE:
### 1. Fill in the skeleton variables below before running, OR
### 2. Copy to 'api.http' (gitignored) and load dynamically from your local .env
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl =
@adminEmail =
@adminPassword =
@adminFirstname =
@adminLastname =
@adminForgotEmail =
@adminUserEmail =
@password =
@hrEmail =
@managerEmail =
@employeeEmail =
@attackerEmail =
@attackerUsername =
@userForgotEmail =
@testEmpName =
@testEmpEmail =
@testEmpMobile =
@testCardId =
@testSalary =

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. ADMINS COLLECTION (/api/admins/*) - Superadmin via admins collection
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 First-register (ONLY works while admins collection is empty)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admins/first-register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}",
  "firstname": "{{adminFirstname}}",
  "lastname": "{{adminLastname}}"
}

### 1.2 Superadmin Login
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admins/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 1.3 Superadmin Forgot Password (always 200; token lands in admins.reset_password_token, 40 chars)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admins/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminForgotEmail}}"
}

### 1.4 Superadmin Reset Password (paste token from DB + fill your own new password; bad token = 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admins/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_HERE",
  "password": ""
}

### 1.5 Superadmin Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admins/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. RBAC ROLE LOGINS (/api/users/login) - seed accounts from README section 3
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Admin-role User Login (role 'admin' in users collection)
# @name adminUserLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminUserEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.2 HR Specialist Login (role 'hr')
# @name hrLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hrEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.3 Department Manager Login (role 'manager')
# @name managerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{managerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.4 Regular Employee Login (role 'employee')
# @name employeeLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{employeeEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. PRIVILEGE ESCALATION DEFENSE (README 5.1 step 1 / OWASP A01 + CWE-269)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Public Register Attack: try to self-assign "role": "admin"
# Expected: 201 Created BUT returned role MUST be "employee" (field access + hook force it)
# @name attackRegister
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{attackerEmail}}",
  "username": "{{attackerUsername}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 3.2 Attacker Login
# @name attackerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{attackerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3.3 Verify Attacker Profile (role must be "employee", NOT "admin")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{attackerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 3.4 Admin Lists Users To Confirm Attacker Role Was Forced Down
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. ROLE: HR SPECIALIST (README 5.1 step 2 - full CRUD, sees salaries)
### Requires seed data: department id 1 + position id 2 must exist (from seed.mjs).
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 HR: List All Employees (200, sees all records + decrypted salary/cardId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 4.2 HR: Create New Employee (201 Allowed for HR)
# @name hrCreateEmployee
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "{{testEmpName}}",
  "email": "{{testEmpEmail}}",
  "mobile": "{{testEmpMobile}}",
  "cardId": "{{testCardId}}",
  "department": 1,
  "position": 2,
  "hireDate": "2024-05-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "salary": "{{testSalary}}"
}

### 4.3 HR: Get Employee By ID (200, salary visible)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{hrCreateEmployee.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 4.4 HR Update Employee Salary (200 Allowed for HR)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{hrCreateEmployee.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "salary": "80000"
}

### 4.5 HR: Attempt To Delete Employee (403 Forbidden - only Superadmin can delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{hrCreateEmployee.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. ROLE: DEPARTMENT MANAGER (README 5.1 step 3 - scoped, PII stripped)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Manager: List Employees (200, scoped to own dept; salary & cardId stripped)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 5.2 Manager: Attempt To Create Employee (403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Unauthorized Add",
  "email": "unauth@example.com",
  "mobile": "0800000000",
  "cardId": "0000000000000",
  "department": 1,
  "position": 1,
  "salary": "0"
}

### 5.3 Manager: Update Employee Mobile In Own Department (200 Allowed - contact info only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "mobile": "0819998877"
}

### 5.4 Manager: Attempt To Tamper With Salary (200 but salary ignored/stripped - HR only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "salary": "999999"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. ROLE: REGULAR EMPLOYEE (README 5.1 step 4 - self-service + directory)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6.1 Employee: Browse Company Directory (200 Allowed, others' salaries hidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 6.2 Employee: View Own Record (200 - sees OWN salary + cardId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees?where[email][equals]={{employeeEmail}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 6.3 Employee: Attempt To Create Employee (403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Fake Employee",
  "email": "fake@example.com",
  "department": 1,
  "position": 1
}

### 6.4 Employee: Attempt To Delete Record (403 Forbidden)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. ROLE: SUPERADMIN (full access - Admins collection or role 'admin')
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 7.1 Admin: List All Users & Roles (200 - Admin/HR only; Manager/Employee get self-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 7.2 Admin: Elevate User Role (200 - only Admin can touch the 'role' field)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "role": "hr"
}

### 7.3 Admin: Delete Employee Record (200 Allowed for Superadmin - cleanup from 4.2)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{hrCreateEmployee.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. DEPARTMENTS (read = any login; write/delete = Admin only)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8.1 Create Department (201 as Superadmin; re-run may 400 duplicate - name is unique)
# @name deptCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Test-Dept-RBAC",
  "description": "RBAC test department"
}

### 8.2 List Departments (200 any authenticated user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 8.3 Get Department By ID (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/departments/{{deptCreate.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 8.4 Update Department (200 as Superadmin)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/departments/{{deptCreate.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "description": "RBAC test department Updated"
}

### 8.5 Employee Tries To Create Department (403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/departments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Illegal Department"
}

### 8.6 Delete Department (200 as Superadmin - cleanup)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/departments/{{deptCreate.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. POSITIONS (read = any login; create/update = Admin/HR; delete = Admin only)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 9.1 HR Creates Position (201 Allowed for HR & Admin)
# @name posCreate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/positions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Test-Position-RBAC",
  "level": "senior",
  "description": "RBAC test position"
}

### 9.2 List Positions (200 any authenticated user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/positions
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 9.3 Get Position By ID (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/positions/{{posCreate.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 9.4 HR Updates Position (200 Allowed for HR & Admin)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/positions/{{posCreate.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "description": "RBAC test position Updated"
}

### 9.5 Employee Tries To Create Position (403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/positions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Illegal Position",
  "level": "junior"
}

### 9.6 Admin Deletes Position (200 - cleanup)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/positions/{{posCreate.response.body.$.doc.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. MEDIA (read = any login; upload = Admin/HR/Manager; delete = Admin only)
### images only (jpeg/png/webp, max 5MB, no pasteURL). Uploads are multipart,
### so the JSON example below is a template - attach a real file in REST Client.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 10.1 List Media (200 any authenticated user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 10.2 HR Uploads Image (201 - multipart/form-data; replace path with a real .png/.jpg)
# In VS Code REST Client: use a multipart body with a file attachment.
# NOTE: Payload reads non-file fields ONLY from the "_payload" JSON part —
# a plain "alt" part is ignored and the request 400s (Alt text is required).
# Expected: 201 as HR; same request as Employee = 403.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----rbac-test-boundary

------rbac-test-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="_payload"
Content-Type: application/json

{"alt": "RBAC test image"}
------rbac-test-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./test.png
------rbac-test-boundary--

### 10.3 Employee Tries To Upload (403 Forbidden - same multipart as HR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/media
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----rbac-test-boundary

------rbac-test-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="_payload"
Content-Type: application/json

{"alt": "Should be rejected"}
------rbac-test-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./test.png
------rbac-test-boundary--

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 11. USERS FORGOT / RESET / PROFILE (kept from pre-RBAC suite)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 11.1 User Forgot Password (always 200; token lands in users.reset_password_token, 40 chars)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userForgotEmail}}"
}

### 11.2 User Reset Password (paste token from DB + fill your own new password; bad token = 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_HERE",
  "password": ""
}

### 11.3 HR Profile (self)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{hrLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 11.4 Employee Profile (self)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.$.token}}
